{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WfrafYM6ctHQCHWK1sQhYc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-13 21:00 +07\n2\t# Task: correct the \"native kernels die at phase 8\" claims (Architect, docs only, mechanical)\n3\tYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends` (branch `docs-backends`, from origin/master). Edit ONLY docs under `docs/design/` and your report `collab/1792460000000-architect-backends-doc-fix.report.md`. No git add/commit. Vocabulary per UCF 7.5.3.\n4\tOwner ruling 2026-10-13 (memory file text): `debruijn/stack.cljc` and `debruijn/register.cljc` are BACKENDS: lowerings of the semantic-register bytecode (A to H stack image, A to R register image), not peers of `yin.vm.semantic-register`, and they are NOT deleted at phase 8. Frozen design section 10 phase 8 deletes only the old `yin.vm.semantic`, `yin.vm.debruijn-resolve`, `debruijn-linearize`, `debruijn-register-compile` (and their tests after replacement coverage), removes `:dim/lift-to` from both de Bruijn descriptors, regenerates H/R, and switches the REPL/linker/publish-closure! to the A-derived lowerings. The reason yin.vm.semantic-register exists is that a register-shaped canonical semantic VM is easier to lower than the old stack-shaped one. The backends support a DOCUMENTED FRAGMENT and are NOT to be widened (no retained-FFI seam, no link/install layout, no free-env closures, no ambiguous-image fix). A lowering must behave identically on what it accepts and refuse before any attach what it cannot represent. Q1 (the 61 law-4 cases and 350 law-5 transfers) stays accepted, but its JUSTIFICATION is \"the supported fragment of a backend\", not \"the kernels die at phase 8\". Q2 (the 6c-post-D2 seam) is closed as rejected by the owner.\n5\tDo: grep all docs under `docs/design/` (continuation design first: it has such claims at about lines 549, 901, 1185, 1415, 2480-2582 incl. section 8.3, the 6c amendments, section 11 Q1/Q2 and any \"bounded by phase 8\", \"removed with their kernels\", \"dies at phase 8\", \"until phase 8 removes those kernels\"; then `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, the semantic-register evaluator/derivations/frozen docs, UCF) for every claim that the de Bruijn kernels, native lanes, the layouts' stack/register halves or the native-lane exclusions are deleted or short-lived at phase 8, and rewrite each so it is TRUE: backends, a documented supported fragment, refusals before attach, kept after phase 8. Where a clause justified a scope reduction by the shelf life, restate the reason (supported fragment) and keep the owner-accepted counts. Mark each edit \"**Amended 2026-10-13 (backends)**\" with a one-line reason. Add a short section to the continuation design (a new subsection in section 4 or section 8) \"The de Bruijn kernels are backends\" stating the model and the fragment (list the five documented limits: ambiguous images, free-environment closures, register-kernel primitives, link/install rows, retained FFI) and the cross-references; close 6c Q2 as rejected, update Q1's rationale. Do not touch code. If any doc says something you cannot decide, list it under open questions. Foreground only. Report: 10-line summary, edits by file and line, open questions. End READY.\n6\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"03d06919-40c9-4cb0-8b1a-0b76373a2601","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:18:24.417Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/collab/1792460000000-architect-backends-doc-fix.prompt.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-13 21:00 +07\n# Task: correct the \"native kernels die at phase 8\" claims (Architect, docs only, mechanical)\nYou are claude-fable-5-1, NEW session. Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends` (branch `docs-backends`, from origin/master). Edit ONLY docs under `docs/design/` and your report `collab/1792