gment, refusals before attach, kept after phase 8. Where a clause justified a scope reduction by the shelf life, restate the reason (supported fragment) and keep the owner-accepted counts. Mark each edit \"**Amended 2026-10-13 (backends)**\" with a one-line reason. Add a short section to the continuation design (a new subsection in section 4 or section 8) \"The de Bruijn kernels are backends\" stating the model and the fragment (list the five documented limits: ambiguous images, free-environment closures, register-kernel primitives, link/install rows, retained FFI) and the cross-references; close 6c Q2 as rejected, update Q1's rationale. Do not touch code. If any doc says something you cannot decide, list it under open questions. Foreground only. Report: 10-line summary, edits by file and line, open questions. End READY.\n","numLines":6,"startLine":1,"totalLines":6}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WfrafYM6ctHQCHWK1sQhYc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
