{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GLeaB4dRXKkN9DwmQxmi5j","type":"tool_result","content":"217\t## 2. The row carrier\n218\t\n219\tThe row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`) is adopted\n220\t**except** where it describes the stack-shaped machine or legacy\n221\treaders; §10.3 lists every replaced or deleted clause. Its §3 (rows, id\n222\tspaces, census, the explicit \"version 3 verifies under BLAKE3\n223\tpermanently\" rule), §4 (value union), §5.1 (value rows, except\n224\t`:reified`), §5.3 (pending), §5.4 (task context, except\n225\t`:parked-table`), §6 (canonical cursor-cell numbering), §7 (equality) and §8\n226\tsteps 1-6 and 8-12 stand.\n227\t\n228\t### 2.1 Positioning: body version 3, one profile\n229\t\n230\t**DECIDED** by ruling 2 and ruling 6. The carrier is **body version 3**.\n231\tVersions 0-2 are the old handoff's; the row reader refuses them at the\n232\tgate (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`) and never reads, normalises or upgrades\n233\tone. Their reader (`yin.vm.ucf.handoff`) is untouched by this phase and\n234\tleaves with the stack-shaped machine at phase 8; that coexistence is\n235\tsequencing, not permission for the row reader to accept a legacy body.\n236\tThe wire unit is the draft's:\n237\t\n238\t```clojure\n239\t{:yin.k/handoff true  :yin.k/version 3  :yin.k/root T  :yin.k/rows [[id kind & slots] …]}\n240\t```\n241\t\n242\t**PROPOSED** (reviewer: ACCEPTED). The profile map is\n243\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}` and nothing else; there is\n244\t**no `:yin.k/engine` key**. The frame is the canonical machine's and\n245\tengine-independent by ruling 6; the kernel that executes it is the\n246\treceiving composition's choice. The version-2 registry"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"94624c41-4f67-4bf1-9db6-240295df37a5","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:18:48.231Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"## 2. The row carrier\n\nThe row-carrier draft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`) is adopted\n**except** where it describes the stack-shaped machine or legacy\nreaders; §10.3 lists every replaced or deleted clause. Its §3 (rows, id\nspaces, census, the explicit \"version 3 verifies under BLAKE3\npermanently\" rule), §4 (value union), §5.1 (value rows, except\n`:reified`), §5.3 (pending), §5.4 (task context, except\n`:parked-table`), §6 (canonical cursor-cell numbering), §7 (equality) and §8\nsteps 1-6 and 8-12 stand.\n\n### 2.1 Positioning: body version 3, one profile\n\n**DECIDED** by ruling 2 and ruling 6. The carrier is **body version 3**.\nVersions 0-2 are the old handoff's; the row reader refuses them at the\ngate (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`) and never reads, normalises or upgrades\none. Their reader (`yin.vm.ucf.handoff`) is untouched by this phase and\nleaves with the stack-shaped machine at phase 8; that coexistence is\nsequencing, not permission for the row reader to accept a legacy body.\nThe wire unit is the draft's:\n\n```clojure\n{:yin.k/handoff true  :yin.k/version 3  :yin.k/root T  :yin.k/rows [[id kind & slots] …]}\n```\n\n**PROPOSED** (reviewer: ACCEPTED). The profile map is\n`{:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}` and nothing else; there is\n**no `:yin.k/engine` key**. The frame is the canonical machine's and\nengine-independent by ruling 6; the kernel that executes it is the\nreceiving composition's choice. The version-2 registry","numLines":30,"startLine":217,"totalLines":2621}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GLeaB4dRXKkN9DwmQxmi5j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
