{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0199VmhFiNoZMBbS89wVB7tt","type":"tool_result","content":"690\t\n691\t**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), the unique-preimage rule for `virt`\n692\t(codex D3, adopted verbatim by R5).** At a reachable boundary, virt\n693\tfirst considers preimages in live-out*. Exactly one is returned. If\n694\tthere are none, it may return the body's sole named virtual preimage,\n695\tsolely to reconstruct a tampered window for validation. Zero or\n696\tmultiple such preimages, or multiple live preimages, are refused as\n697\t:yin.k/non-portable :register-layout; no enumeration order selects a\n698\tpreimage. The harness checks an ambiguous dead physical slot is\n699\trefused, a unique dead slot yields :window-extra through the frame\n700\tvalidator, and a missing live slot yields :window-missing. *What the\n701\tcode does:* `layout/virt` filters the body's `phys` map for `s` over\n702\tthe sorted `live-out*` set, answers the one live preimage, else the one\n703\tnamed preimage when no live one exists, else refuses with `{:yin.k/pc p\n704\t:yin.k/register s}`. *Why:* the restricted inverse of the paragraph\n705\tabove left a tampered-upward `live` with no reconstruction at all\n706\t(engineer deviation 7), and codex's M9 (take the first of several\n707\tpreimages) survived the suite until `harness/layout-refusals` pinned\n708\tthe ambiguous case over C's reused slots (§8.3 item 12). The fallback\n709\tis a diagnostic extension, not a layout claim, and lives only until\n710\tphase 8.\n711\t\n712\t**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), primitives in the register kernel's\n713\tpayload (codex D4, adopted verbatim by R6).** A primitive function is\n714\tan admitted carrier value (:prim). The current de Bruijn register"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"5bba7ece-5bef-4d3a-9fa4-2455fd3c878b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:18:50.756Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"\n**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), the unique-preimage rule for `virt`\n(codex D3, adopted verbatim by R5).** At a reachable boundary, virt\nfirst considers preimages in live-out*. Exactly one is returned. If\nthere are none, it may return the body's sole named virtual preimage,\nsolely to reconstruct a tampered window for validation. Zero or\nmultiple such preimages, or multiple live preimages, are refused as\n:yin.k/non-portable :register-layout; no enumeration order selects a\npreimage. The harness checks an ambiguous dead physical slot is\nrefused, a unique dead slot yields :window-extra through the frame\nvalidator, and a missing live slot yields :window-missing. *What the\ncode does:* `layout/virt` filters the body's `phys` map for `s` over\nthe sorted `live-out*` set, answers the one live preimage, else the one\nnamed preimage when no live one exists, else refuses with `{:yin.k/pc p\n:yin.k/register s}`. *Why:* the restricted inverse of the paragraph\nabove left a tampered-upward `live` with no reconstruction at all\n(engineer deviation 7), and codex's M9 (take the first of several\npreimages) survived the suite until `harness/layout-refusals` pinned\nthe ambiguous case over C's reused slots (§8.3 item 12). The fallback\nis a diagnostic extension, not a layout claim, and lives only until\nphase 8.\n\n**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), primitives in the register kernel's\npayload (codex D4, adopted verbatim by R6).** A primitive function is\nan admitted carrier value (:prim). The current de Bruijn register","numLines":25,"startLine":690,"totalLines":2621}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0199VmhFiNoZMBbS89wVB7tt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
