{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3aMabtfAKQh9UTJmwTNeT","type":"tool_result","content":"1395\t  (`semantic_register.cljc:24`, set once in `create-vm` `:394`, a gc root\n1396\t  `:489`). `lift-task*` takes `(:free-env opts)` when supplied, else the\n1397\t  kernel's `(:free-env m)`, and refuses `:yin.k/non-portable\n1398\t  :missing-free-env` only when neither exists. The explicit value\n1399\t  **overrides** the field without comparing against it; an override the\n1400\t  carried `E`s disagree with is caught by E2 when the lift validates its\n1401\t  own frames (`:yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state`, e.g. `{x 5}`\n1402\t  against an `E` holding `x 99` off the lexical names). Install children\n1403\t  are lifted with the `:free-env` option removed, so a child always reads\n1404\t  its own kernel field.\n1405\t\n1406\tMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n1407\t`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\n1408\tusually already exists.\n1409\t\n1410\t**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), closures and continuations in the free\n1411\tenvironment on the native lanes (R3).** A de Bruijn kernel resolves free\n1412\tnames through its single `free-env` while a canonical closure snapshots\n1413\tits `env`; a closure or continuation held in the free environment\n1414\ttherefore has no finite canonical form on a de Bruijn kernel. Until\n1415\tphase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses such a value in the carried\n1416\t`free-env` before attach (`:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value`, with the\n1417\tpath), and a de Bruijn source refuses it at lift before serving. The\n1418\tcarrier and the semantic-register kernel admit it. *What the code does:*\n1419\t`lower-defect`'s third clause (`free-env-procedure`) walks the root's\n1420\t`free-env` bindings row in its sorted order and the `:vec`, `:list`,\n1421\t`:set` and `:map` rows under each value, and refuses the first\n1422\t`:closure` or `:reified` row it reaches with `:yin.k/path [:free-env sym\n1423\t…]` (indices appended through collections, e.g. `[:free-env box 1 0]`);\n1424\t`canonical-task` refuses `:yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"5dfec7a1-a2c8-4635-b819-0a926fffd203","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:18:54.680Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"  (`semantic_register.cljc:24`, set once in `create-vm` `:394`, a gc root\n  `:489`). `lift-task*` takes `(:free-env opts)` when supplied, else the\n  kernel's `(:free-env m)`, and refuses `:yin.k/non-portable\n  :missing-free-env` only when neither exists. The explicit value\n  **overrides** the field without comparing against it; an override the\n  carried `E`s disagree with is caught by E2 when the lift validates its\n  own frames (`:yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state`, e.g. `{x 5}`\n  against an `E` holding `x 99` off the lexical names). Install children\n  are lifted with the `:free-env` option removed, so a child always reads\n  its own kernel field.\n\nMerkle sharing means every `E` whose bindings equal another's shares one\n`:bindings` row; the root slot is one more reference to a row that\nusually already exists.\n\n**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), closures and continuations in the free\nenvironment on the native lanes (R3).** A de Bruijn kernel resolves free\nnames through its single `free-env` while a canonical closure snapshots\nits `env`; a closure or continuation held in the free environment\ntherefore has no finite canonical form on a de Bruijn kernel. Until\nphase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses such a value in the carried\n`free-env` before attach (`:yin.k/unsupported :free-env-value`, with the\npath), and a de Bruijn source refuses it at lift before serving. The\ncarrier and the semantic-register kernel admit it. 