{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q4GM8Jt86rPq6VMF67Nkjs","type":"tool_result","content":"712\t**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), primitives in the register kernel's\n713\tpayload (codex D4, adopted verbatim by R6).** A primitive function is\n714\tan admitted carrier value (:prim). The current de Bruijn register\n715\tkernel cannot restore a primitive function reachable through its saved\n716\tregister or lexical-frame payload, including nested guest collections,\n717\tclosure captures and reified continuation state. Lowering a task with\n718\tsuch a wait or parked-state payload into that kernel refuses\n719\t:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers, with the payload path,\n720\tbefore stream attachment. This restriction does not prohibit\n721\tprimitives in the task-wide free environment or in carrier values a\n722\tkernel can otherwise hold. Cross-engine acceptance explicitly records\n723\tunsupported payload cases; expanding this receiver domain requires a\n724\tseparate kernel seam. *What the code does:* `lower-defect`'s register\n725\tclause (`state-prim` over every `:wait` row's state, path `[:frames i\n726\t…]`, then every parked-table state, path `[:parked P …]`) finds the\n727\tfirst `:prim` row reachable through a window (`… :window r`), a lexical\n728\tbinding of an `:env` (`… :env sym`, only the names the chain binds at\n729\tthat pc; the free part of `E` is the kernel's `:free-env` and is\n730\texempt), a closure's lexical bindings (`… :env sym …`), a reified\n731\tstate's act, and the elements of `:vec`, `:list`, `:set` and `:map`\n732\trows (index appended). The stack kernel has no such limit and holds\n733\tthe same carriers (`harness/layout-refusals` runs each refused program\n734\tinto the stack lane and checks the reference value). *Why:* the register\n735\tkernel's restore refuses primitives in registers (`vm/machine-data?`,\n736\t`:continuation-registers`); the refusal belongs before attachment and\n737\tin the layout, not in the carrier (engineer deviation 8).\n738\t\n739\t### 4.3 The stack kernel's layout\n740\t\n741\t**DECIDED** by phase-5 §3.2 (the emitter's walk) and the kernel's call"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"ff8f8e2a-98ff-4822-bc66-282f47e0811a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:19:08.178Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"**Amended after 6c (2026-10-13), primitives in the register kernel's\npayload (codex D4, adopted verbatim by R6).** A primitive function is\nan admitted carrier value (:prim). The current de Bruijn register\nkernel cannot restore a primitive function reachable through its saved\nregister or lexical-frame payload, including nested guest collections,\nclosure captures and reified continuation state. Lowering a task with\nsuch a wait or parked-state payload into that kernel refuses\n:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers, with the payload path,\nbefore stream attachment. This restriction does not prohibit\nprimitives in the task-wide free environment or in carrier values a\nkernel can otherwise hold. Cross-engine acceptance explicitly records\nunsupported payload cases; expanding this receiver domain requires a\nseparate kernel seam. *What the code does:* `lower-defect`'s register\nclause (`state-prim` over every `:wait` row's state, path `[:frames i\n…]`, then every parked-table state, path `[:parked P …]`) finds the\nfirst `:prim` row reachable through a window (`… :window r`), a lexical\nbinding of an `:env` (`… :env sym`, only the names the chain binds at\nthat pc; the free part of `E` is the kernel's `:free-env` and is\nexempt), a closure's lexical bindings (`… :env sym …`), a reified\nstate's act, and the elements of `:vec`, `:list`, `:set` and `:map`\nrows (index appended). The stack kernel has no such limit and holds\nthe same carriers (`harness/layout-refusals` runs each refused program\ninto the stack lane and checks the reference value). *Why:* the register\nkernel's restore refuses primitives in registers (`vm/machine-data?`,\n`:continuation-registers`); the refusal belongs before attachment and\nin the layout, not in the carrier (engineer deviation 8).\n\n### 4.3 The stack kernel's layout\n\n**DECIDED** by phase-5 §3.2 (the emitter's walk) and the kernel's call","numLines":30,"startLine":712,"totalLines":2621}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q4GM8Jt86rPq6VMF67Nkjs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
