{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015BVJXyyqcbFsPREdpjDvxt","type":"tool_result","content":"2012\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n2013\t\n2014\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n2015\t|---|---|---|\n2016\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n2017\t| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n2018\t| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n2019\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n2020\t\n2021\tNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n2022\t`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\n2023\tregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\n2024\tnot edited. **Amended after 6c (2026-10-13):** 6c proper held to this:\n2025\tit created `layout.cljc` and `layout_test.cljc`, extended the 6b harness\n2026\tfile and the store-write audit's allowlist, and edited no kernel, no\n2027\t`rows.cljc` and no 4b or phase-5 file. The one further kernel edit this\n2028\tdesign names, the retained-FFI response-pair seam of both de Bruijn\n2029\tkernels (§4.3, 6c-post-D2), is its own slice behind an owner decision\n2030\t(§11, 6c Q2) and is not part of 6c.\n2031\t\n2032\t---\n2033\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"553b824c-62b3-4f6f-a68d-09230a1c509d","uuid":"ed7b3572-d49c-42e8-a575-c54da1c2389a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:19:09.113Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-backends/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\nnot edited. **Amended after 6c (2026-10-13):** 6c proper held to this:\nit created `layout.cljc` and `layout_test.cljc`, extended the 6b harness\nfile and the store-write audit's allowlist, and edited no kernel, no\n`rows.cljc` and no 4b or phase-5 file. The one further kernel edit this\ndesign names, the retained-FFI response-pair seam of both de Bruijn\nkernels (§4.3, 6c-post-D2), is its own slice behind an owner decision\n(§11, 6c Q2) and is not part of 6c.\n\n---\n","numLines":22,"startLine":2012,"totalLines":2621}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015BVJXyyqcbFsPREdpjDvxt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
